According to previous posts:
The format of the save file depends on what options are on, and, if I remember
correctly, what order things were compiled in.  This means two things:

1) You cannot restore a saved game if any options have been changed by the
recompile.

2) If you do recompile, and the new version is different from the old in any
way, shape, or form, the save file, while loadable, will be corrupted.
(Someone had this a while back.  The inventory was QUITE amusing.)

As for a discussion of the HARD option:
It is, IMO, realistic.  Do you remember things which take a lot of energy out
of you when you try to recall them?  It's Pavlovian (sp?) conditioning-you
are tired out by reciting a spell, so you forget it in order to conserve
energy. :-)  Seriously, though, it would be too easy if you found a spellbook
or remove curse and removed every curse from every item you came across.  Or
if you just cast fireballs and magic missles at everything.  There's a reason
it's the HARD option.

And some people suggest an ExtraHard option.  The masochists.  But my vote's
with them: The only way to keep the game interesting is to make it harder.

If you don't wish to play with the HARD option, but don't wish to loose your
spellbooks, you've got a problem.  In the future, be prepared to live with
whatever options you start with.

